Interactive USD edits of point instancers with deduplicated curves prototypes (HDARNOLD_GEOM_DEDUP=1)

Two point instancers have identical linear curves prototypes, which the render delegate deduplicates in mode 1 (the
default, identical point instancer prototypes share their arnold geometry). The points of one prototype are set again
to the same values, its displayColor and points are edited, becoming different from the other one and identical
again, and the other point instancer is removed. The stage is re-rendered after each edit. Covers the fix of the dedup
incremental updates (#2797).
The scenario runs with the "usd" procedural (hydra reader) reading the stage through its cache_id in an interactive
render session, and with the HdArnoldRendererPlugin render delegate driven like a Hydra host, see
testsuite/common/interactive_usd_test.h. Each render is checked in test.cpp, and the last procedural render is
compared against the reference image. Edits that aren't rendered correctly yet are reported as warnings (known issues
in test.cpp).

author: sebastien.blaineau.ortega@autodesk.com

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'interactive_usd'}
